  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two conductors have the same resistances at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo> </mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> but their temperature coefficients of resistance are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. The respective temperature coefficients for their series and parallel combinations are :</p>",
    "image": null
  },
